    "created_at": "2025-06-19T02:44:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-19T02:45:48Z",
    "body": "I built a simple browser-based flash detection tool using JavaScript and canvas. It analyzes real-time brightness fluctuations in video and raises an alert when rapid flashing occurs.\n\nYou can run it entirely client-side, as long as CORS issues are handled (e.g. via localhost).\n\nThis could serve as a baseline for accessibility testing (e.g., for epilepsy-triggering flashes), or be adapted into a user-uploaded video safety checker.\n\nHere's the script: \n`<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <title>Flash Detection Debug</title>\n  <style>\n    #alert { font-weight: bold; color: gray; margin-top: 10px; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<h2>Flashing Video Detector (Debug Mode)</h2>\n<video id=\"video\" width=\"480\" controls muted crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n  <source src=\"videoplayback.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\">\n</video>\n\n<div id=\"alert\">Waiting for video...</div>\n<canvas id=\"canvas\" style=\"display:none;\"></canvas>\n\n<script>\nconst video = document.getElementById(\"video\");\nconst canvas = document.getElementById(\"canvas\");\nconst ctx = canvas.getContext(\"2d\");\nconst alert = document.getElementById(\"alert\");\n\nlet lastBrightness = null;\nlet flashTimestamps = [];\n\nfunction getBrightness() {\n  const width = 160, height = 90;\n  canvas.width = width;\n  canvas.height = height;\n\n  try {\n    ctx.drawImage(video, 0, 0, width, height);\n    const frame = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, width, height).data;\n\n    let sum = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < frame.length; i += 4) {\n      const r = frame[i], g = frame[i + 1], b = frame[i + 2];\n      const brightness = 0.299 * r + 0.587 * g + 0.114 * b;\n      sum += brightness;\n    }\n\n    return sum / (frame.length / 4);\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.warn(\"Frame read failed:\", e);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction detectFlashes() {\n  const brightness = getBrightness();\n  if (brightness === null) {\n    alert.textContent = \"⚠️ Unable to read video frame (CORS or video not ready)\";\n    alert.style.color = \"orange\";\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const now = Date.now();\n  if (lastBrightness !== null && Math.abs(brightness - lastBrightness) > 20) {\n    flashTimestamps.push(now);\n  }\n\n  flashTimestamps = flashTimestamps.filter(t => now - t < 1000);\n  lastBrightness = brightness;\n\n  if (flashTimestamps.length > 3) {\n    alert.textContent = \" Flashing detected!\";\n    alert.style.color = \"red\";\n  } else {\n    alert.textContent = \"No flashing detected.\";\n    alert.style.color = \"green\";\n  }\n}\n\n// Ensure playback\nvideo.muted = true;\n\nvideo.addEventListener(\"canplay\", () => {\n  console.log(\"Video is ready to play.\");\n  video.play();\n});\n\nvideo.addEventListener(\"playing\", () => {\n  alert.textContent = \"Analyzing video...\";\n  setInterval(detectFlashes, 100);\n});\n</script>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n`\nbelow the tested video\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B4wSFjR9TMQ\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3b670556-f06e-4db2-9b23-0dd22162f22b)",
